<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Magdeburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Magdeburg is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Otto I made it a centre of his rule and raised it to an archbishopric in 968, and its town law, Magdeburg law, was adopted by hundreds of towns across central and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Its sack in 1631 was one of the worst massacres of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/magdeburg.jpg" alt="Magdeburg" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Olivier Cleynen · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_Magdeburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
